<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Gomma</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 CE – 1886 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the five Oromo kingdoms of the Gibe region in south-western Ethiopia, noted as an early centre of Islam among the Oromo.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gomma emerged around 1800 in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/didessa-river">Didessa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibe-river">Gibe</a> valleys, one of the monarchies formed as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oromo">Oromo</a> settlers of the region replaced the egalitarian gadaa system with hereditary kingship. It bordered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-jimma">Kingdom of Jimma</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/limmu-ennarea">Limmu-Ennarea</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gumma">Kingdom of Gumma</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gera">Kingdom of Gera</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings ruled through officials and governors in the manner of the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibe-river">Gibe</a> states, and its people farmed and grew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> in the fertile valleys. Gomma was among the first Gibe states to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, and Muslim scholars and traders from the north were active there. It took part in the trade in coffee, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and slaves.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Weakened by wars with its neighbours, Gomma was conquered by the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> and annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> in 1886.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-gomma.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Gomma" width="320" height="289"><figcaption>Image: LeGabrie · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gibe_kingdoms.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 CE – 1886 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oromo</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gomma</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1843&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gomma" aria-label="Kingdom of Gomma on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5692 1884 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Gomma lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6012 2140L6029 1964"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6029 1964h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6012 2140h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6012 2140h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1843&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gomma">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

